# Vendored quire output schemas (FR-029). These are copies of quire-rs's
# published artifacts and must match them BYTE FOR BYTE — their SHA-256 is
# recorded in src/quire/contract.ts and asserted on every test run. Formatting
# them locally rewrites the bytes and breaks the provenance check, which is
# exactly how a vendored contract drifts by default. Refresh them with
# scripts/refresh-quire-schemas.mjs, never with prettier.
src/quire/schemas/

# Real tool output, captured unedited (agent-ix/quoin#115). The ticket asked
# for the format decisions to be made "by reading real output from each tool,
# not from the spec of the format", so a fixture reformatted to house style is
# no longer the thing it was captured to be. Same reasoning as the vendored
# quire schemas above: these bytes are evidence, not source.
tests/fixtures/evidence/
